===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The act of physically [[applying]] or [[lay on|laying on]].
#: {{ux|en|The '''application''' of this cream should reduce the swelling.}}
# The substance applied.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1857|author=John Eadie; John Francis Waller; William John Macquorn Rankine|title=The Imperial Dictionary of Universal Biography
|passage=His body was stripped, laid out upon a table, and covered with a hearsecloth, when some of his attendants perceived symptoms of returning animation, and by the use of warm '''applications''', internal and external, gradually restored him to life.}}
# The act of applying as a [[means]]; the employment of means to accomplish an [[end]]; [[specific]] use.
#* {{RQ:Locke Education|43
|passage=All that I have hitherto contended for, is, that whatsoever rigor is necessary, it is more to be us'd, the younger children are; and having by a due '''application''' wrought its effect, it is to be relax'd, and chang'd into a milder sort of government.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Popular Woodworking|date=August 2026|volume=290|number=4|title=Omtech 60W Autofocus MOPA Fiber Laser|author=Logan Wittmer|page=10
|text=What sets fiber lasers apart is their ability to mark (engrave) metal, which opens up a range of possibilities as a complement to woodworking. Brass nameplates for awards or plaques are an obvious '''application''', but it goes further than that.}}
# The act of [[direct]]ing or [[refer]]ring something to a [[particular]] case, to discover or illustrate [[agreement]] or [[disagreement]], [[fitness]], or [[correspondence]].
#: {{ux|en|I make the remark, and leave you to make the '''application'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''application''' of a theory to a set of data can be challenging.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q40056}}{{lb|en|computing}} A [[computer program]] or the [[set]] of [[software]] that the [[end user]] perceives as a single entity as a tool for a well-defined purpose. (Also called: [[application program]]; [[application software]].)
#: {{ux|en|This '''application''' can connect to most social networks.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|author={{w|Mohsin Hamid}}|title=''{{w|Exit West}}''|publisher=Hamish Hamilton|page=15|passage=Saeed straightened and held up his phone, directing its camera at the heavens, consulting an '''application''' that indicated the names of celestial bodies he did not know.}}
# A verbal or written request for [[assistance]] or [[employment]] or [[admission]] to a [[school]], [[course]] or similar.
#: {{ux|en|December 31 is the deadline for MBA '''applications'''.}}
# {{lb|en|bureaucracy|legal}} A [[petition]], [[entreaty]], or other [[request]], with the adposition [[for]] denoting the subject matter.
#: {{ux|en|Their '''application''' for a deferral of the hearing was granted.}}
# The act of requesting, claiming, or petitioning something.
#: {{ux|en|Specimen copies may be obtained on '''application''' to the publisher.}} 
# [[diligence|Diligence]]; close thought or attention.
# A kind of [[needlework]]; [[appliqué]].
# {{lb|en|comptheory}} The [[substitution]] of a [[specific]] [[value]] for the [[parameter]] in the [[abstraction]], in [[lambda calculus]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[compliance|Compliance]].

